WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.740
A Quiet Place is packed with many tense, nerve-shredding
moments, however, one special scene between

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:12.080
John Krasinski and Emily Blunt is loaded with
much more meaning than you might realise.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.410
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm taking a deep dive into A Quiet

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:21.029
Place to explain the secret story behind the
movie's earbud scene and why director John

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:24.289
Krasinski insisted it had to be in the movie.

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:26.939
Spoilers ahead if you haven't seen the film
yet!

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:31.730
In the earbud scene, Emily Blunt's Evelyn
and her husband Lee take a moment for a slow

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.850
dance together and, in doing so, briefly tune
out the horror of their everyday life hiding

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.730
from the sound-sensitive aliens that threaten
them.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:44.149
It's a very tender moment and, as the two
parents sway together, Evelyn takes out one

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:47.630
of her earbuds and shares the song she's listening
to with Lee.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.850
The song is "Harvest Moon" by Neil Young and
it's the only song that plays in the movie.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.719
The curious thing about this song choice is
that it's a very expensive song to license

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:01.219
and, given the film's tight budget, it wasn't
something the production could really afford.

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:05.820
However, for Krasinski, who wrote this scene
as part of his rewrite of the original script,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.650
it was vital to have this specific song in
the movie.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:14.500
According to producer Andrew Form, Krasinksi
"would not stop until we got that song."

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.210
So, why was it so important for Krasinski
to play this expensive song in his relatively

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.550
low-budget movie?

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:25.810
Well, first of all, it's a very personal track
for Krasinski and his real-life wife, Emily

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.290
Blunt, as two of their close friends got married
to the song.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:33.130
In fact, on the first take the couple shot
of that intimate scene, Krasinski looked up

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.340
and saw not only he and Blunt "were crying
at the exact same time", but their crew were

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.260
also welling up.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.230
And beyond that personal connection, there
are also multiple levels of meaning to the

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.560
song itself.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.840
Neil Young, who wrote and performed "Harvest
Moon", has said that it's about "this feeling,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.460
this ability to survive and continue and grow
and get higher than you were before.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:59.190
[…] You can be MORE alive" which, as I explained
in my Quiet Place ending video, is a key theme

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:04.360
in the movie – how a family not only survives
an alien invasion, but aims to thrive and

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.030
grow in spite of it.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:10.700
Over the years since its release though, some
have interpreted the song as more bittersweet,

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.860
being about a love that endures even when
a couple are no longer together.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.160
The line "When we were lovers, I loved you
with all my heart" could hint at two people

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.890
who are separated.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.640
And so the song could foreshadow the heartbreaking
events later in the movie when Lee sacrifices

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.660
himself to save his family, with the lyrics
implying that Lee and Evelyn will still remain

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.670
connected in spirit even though he's gone.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:38.460
On top of that, a Harvest Moon is the full
moon that occurs closest to the autumn equinox,

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.980
and usually coincides with the September or
October full moon.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:47.150
And, as we see on the family's calendar, the
due date for the Abbots' new baby is the day

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.170
before the October full moon.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:54.260
Traditionally, the Harvest Moon also had special
meaning for rural communities, like in A Quiet

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:59.120
Place, because it meant there was plenty of
moonlight even after sunset which helped when

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.480
harvesting crops at that time of year.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.350
And it fits in with the idea of the seasons
of life, again foreshadowing how Lee's life

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.260
will be coming to an end.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.540
All-in-all, the song is a bittersweet and
tender moment for the couple as they savour

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.850
some brief time together and anticipate the
arrival of their new baby.

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:21.569
It's also an instant of respite for the audience
watching the movie as the silence fades out

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:25.770
and we can relax with a gentle song before
the full horror of the family's fate kicks

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.770
in.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:30.210
And adding another layer of meaning to the
song is the fact that Neil Young made his

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:35.620
Harvest Moon album at a time when he was suffering
from tinnitus and couldn't listen to any loud

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.620
noises.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:40.840
Young had damaged his hearing while working
on an earlier album and concert tour, which

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.280
makes the song even more appropriate for A
Quiet Place.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:49.350
Now, just for a bit of fun, fans of John Krasinski
in The Office may also link the Quiet Place

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:53.760
earbud scene with the time that Jim shared
his earbuds with Pam in a similarly romantic

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.060
moment in season 2 of the popular show.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:00.310
I don't know whether Krasinski had that sweet
Jim and Pam moment in mind when he wrote this

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.480
scene in A Quiet Place, but either way it's
a nice call-back for fans of the show.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.500
So, did you spot any other hidden meanings
in A Quiet Place and what do you think about

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.680
the earbud scene?

